GroundTruthIdeaExtraction.user_prompt_template:
Extract the paper's ground-truth strategy categories for downstream evaluation.

Title: {title}
Journal: {journal}
Date: {date}
DOI: {doi}

Paper snippet:
{snippet}

Your extraction must include only the paper's major regulation strategies under the required tuning dimensions.

Return valid JSON with exactly this schema:
{
  "strategy_categories": {
    "Composition Tuning": [],
    "Interface Tuning": [],
    "Stress Tuning": [],
    "Texture Tuning": [],
    "Grain Boundary Tuning": []
  }
}

Field requirements:
- strategy_categories: only the major regulation strategies that define the paper's core idea.
- You must inspect all five tuning dimensions and return the full supported strategy set across these five categories; do not omit any major supported strategy.
- You must return the full five-category structure exactly as shown in the schema.
- Each strategy item should be a concise but specific tuning-strategy statement, not just a bare keyword.
- Put each strategy into the single best-fitting tuning dimension.

Important constraints:
- Do not output a paper summary.
- Do not include markdown fences.
- Do not add extra fields.
- Return valid JSON only.

GroundTruthExperimentExtraction.user_prompt_template:
I will provide you with a research paper about REBCO flux pinning. Please analyze the paper and extract both: 1. the paper idea as conceptual input for baseline systems; 2. the paper experiment as the ground-truth experimental label. Requirements: use English for all fields; every field must be directly supported by the paper; do not hallucinate missing information; if a parameter is not explicitly reported, omit it instead of guessing; keep `paper_idea` conceptual rather than fully executable; keep `paper_experiment` focused on the actual implemented experiment; do not include `paper_name`; do not include `regulation_strategies` inside `paper_experiment`; output only the JSON object wrapped in <template> and </template>.

Paper metadata:
Title: {title}
Journal: {journal}
Date: {date}
DOI: {doi}

Paper text:
{snippet}

Return exactly this schema:
<template>
{{
  "paper_idea": {{
    "material": "",
    "motivation": "",
    "strategies": [
      {{
        "tuning dimensions": "",
        "tuning strategies": "",
        "tuning effects": ""
      }}
    ],
    "technique": "",
    "outcome": ""
  }},
  "paper_experiment": {{
    "material_system": "",
    "experimental_goal": "",
    "fabrication_process": "",
    "key_parameters": {{}},
    "characterization": "",
    "outcome": "",
    "experiment_logic": ""
  }}
}}
</template>
